# Cursor AI Rules for Shark Vision Project

## Documentation Policy
- NEVER proactively create documentation files (*.md) or README files after changes
- Only create or update documentation when explicitly requested by the user
- Do not create summary documents, change logs, or update notes unless asked

## Code Reuse Policy
- ALWAYS search for and reuse existing components, utilities, and code before creating new ones
- Check the codebase thoroughly using codebase_search or grep before implementing new functionality
- If similar functionality exists, extend or modify it rather than duplicating
- Prefer refactoring existing code over creating parallel implementations
- When a component already exists that can be adapted, modify it instead of creating a new one

## Development Preferences
- Prioritize editing existing files over creating new files
- Use the component structure already established in the project
- Follow existing patterns and conventions found in the codebase
- Keep the codebase DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)

## File Organization
- Place new components in `/components` directory only if they don't already exist
- Check for existing utilities before creating new helper functions
- Consolidate related functionality into existing modules when possible

## Body Language Analysis Module
- Core logic in `lib/body_language/` - do not duplicate
- Event detection thresholds in `metrics.ts` - single source of truth
- Video recording handled by `lib/video_recorder.ts` - reuse this class
- Storage operations in `lib/storage.ts` - use these functions

## TypeScript Standards
- Use strict typing throughout
- Import types from `lib/body_language/types.ts`
- Avoid `any` types - use proper interfaces
- Client components must have 'use client' directive

## Performance Considerations
- TensorFlow.js processing is expensive - maintain 10 FPS target
- Video files can be large - use appropriate bitrates
- Browser memory management - dispose of unused resources

## Future Integration Points
- Audio analysis: `lib/audio_analyzer.ts` (not yet implemented)
- Slide detection: `lib/slide_detector.ts` (not yet implemented)
- LLM coaching: `app/api/coaching/route.ts` (not yet implemented)

## Communication
- Focus responses on code changes and technical implementation
- Skip verbose explanations about what was changed unless specifically asked
- Do not create change summaries or documentation after completing tasks
